{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And the magicians did so.</b> They attempted to do so." "<b>And they could not.</b> For all the dust was lice. And from where would lice come to them? And one may say, <b>to bring out their lice</b> — to eliminate them, and therefore they attempted to eliminate them, for in this way people would notice; but to bring them, as Aaron did, they did not attempt, for all the dust of the earth was already lice. Another interpretation: <b>and they could not</b> — they could not stand, each man before his fellow, because of the shame, for they were full of lice, as with the boils, that they were full of boils. Another interpretation: <b>and they could not</b> — for all the dust of the earth was lice and their feet did not touch the ground, and as long as a sorcerer's feet are not touching, his sorcery does not succeed. <b>And they could not</b> — even though with blood and frogs they did as Moses and Aaron did, nevertheless they did not eliminate them; with the third plague, He did not give them power either to make or to eliminate, so that they would not be established in the matter; and when they saw that they could not, they said, 'It is the finger of Elohim,' and did not perform sorcery. And the reason is not because a demon has no dominion over anything smaller than a barley grain, for if so, why could they not bring out the mixed swarms?"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:38.126039813Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}